Package: epiforest
Type: Package
Title: Random Forest Screening for Epistatic Interactions in Case-Control Studies
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("fossil contributors", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "noreply@github.com",
    comment = "jeonglab-bcm/fossil; method by Jiang R, Tang W, Wu X and Fu W (2009)")
Description: The two-stage epiForest method of Jiang, Tang, Wu and Fu (2009)
    <doi:10.1186/1471-2105-10-S1-S65>: a random forest ranks single nucleotide
    polymorphisms (SNPs) by gini importance, a sliding window sequential forward
    feature selection (SWSFS) picks the candidates that minimise the out-of-bag
    error, and a hierarchical procedure tests one-, two- and three-way
    interactions among the candidates with the B statistic of Zhang and Liu
    (2007) <doi:10.1038/ng2110>. Also the paper's simulation design (the disease
    models of Marchini, Donnelly and Cardon (2005) <doi:10.1038/ng1537>) and its
    comparators (single-locus chi-squared test, stepwise logistic regression).
    Rebuilt from the paper's text; the authors' program is lost.
